\ ff-test: lines
\ Real literals: digits with a fraction and/or an exponent, '.' as the
\ decimal point whatever the host's locale (see the API test for that).
\
\ A value too small to be represented normally was rejected, because
\ strtod() reports underflow the way it reports overflow; and `-inf` and
\ `-nan` read as reals where `inf` and `nan` didn't.

: p 32 emit f. ;
1.5 p  -2.25e-1 p  1. p  -.5 p  2E3 p cr
1e-310 p cr

\ Not reals: too large, no digits, no exponent digits, inf and nan.
1e400
-e5
1e
-inf
nan
clear

\ `see` prints a real so that it reads back as the same value.
: r 0.1 -2.5e-7 1e300 ;
see r
